<td id="S4.T1.1.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Skewness of <math id="S4.T1.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{norm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{norm}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{verti}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{verti}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T1.m65" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{49}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>49</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{49}</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S4.T1.m66" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{51}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>51</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{51}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Correlation coefficient between each pair of <math id="S4.T1.m67" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m68" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m69" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{z}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.1.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S4.T1.m70" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{52}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>52</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{52}</annotation></semantics></math>-<math id="S4.T1.m71" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{54}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>54</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{54}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S4.T1.1.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Correlation coefficient between each pair of <math id="S4.T1.m72" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{norm}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{norm}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m73" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{verti}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{verti}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.T1.m74" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS3.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span>3 </span>Min-Max Normalization</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Once the impact-defined window is determined, the data is processed using min-max normalization to reduce scaling effects during the training phase. By applying min-max normalization, each element of the data sequence <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S=\{s_{i}|i=1,2\cdots,I\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{s_{i}|i=1,2\cdots,I\}</annotation></semantics></math> is normalized to a range between 0 and 1, which is shown as</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{nom}=\frac{s_{i}-s_{min}}{s_{max}-s_{min}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{nom}=\frac{s_{i}-s_{min}}{s_{max}-s_{min}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{min}</annotation></semantics></math> are the maximum and minimum values of <math id="S4.SS1.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
In addition, we have compared min-max normalization and z-score standardization (standard scalar standardization) in our experiments for fall detection.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Threshold-Based Classification</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our study, we categorized all human actions into ADLs and falls. The features of falls and ADLs are extracted by the threshold-based classification. An initial threshold-based detection using maximum and minimum spatial momentum values is employed. The maximum and minimum spatial momentum values are determined by two types of data features, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math>, that are extracted from each data frame. <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated by Eq. (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In IV-A1 Impact-Defined Window ‣ IV-A Data Pre-Processing ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and characterizes the spatial variation of acceleration during the falling interval.
<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the Euclidean norm of acceleration for capturing the change of velocity in the horizontal plane of the body and is calculated as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}(S_{j})=\sqrt{a_{y_{j}}^{2}+a_{z_{j}}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}(S_{j})=\sqrt{a_{y_{j}}^{2}+a_{z_{j}}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The threshold is determined by the maximum and minimum values of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> as shown in Fig. <a href="#S4.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ IV-B Threshold-Based Classification ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
Fig. <a href="#S4.F5" title="Fig. 5 ‣ IV-B Threshold-Based Classification ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> distributions of falls and ADLs, where the left seven activities are falls and the right twelve activities are ADLs, the green line is determined by the maximum value of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math>) of ADLs, and the purple line is determined by the minimum value of <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math>) of falls.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.03601v1/ADLa.png" id="S4.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/145;" width="234" height="145" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.03601v1/ADLb.png" id="S4.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/145;" width="234" height="145" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 5: </span>The illustration of the <math id="S4.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> distribution of falls and ADLs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>, <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> (a) The boxplots of maximum and minimum values of <math id="S4.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> for falls and ADLs; (b) The boxplots of maximum and minimum values of <math id="S4.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Assume that there is a training set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{train}=\{(f_{i}^{train})|i=1,2\cdots,N_{train}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{train}=\{(f_{i}^{train})|i=1,2\cdots,N_{train}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{train}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number data frames, and there is a testing set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{test}=\{(f_{i}^{test})|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{test}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{test}=\{(f_{i}^{test})|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{test}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{test}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of the set <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{test}</annotation></semantics></math>, two sets of maximum <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{train}</annotation></semantics></math> are presented as <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{train}=\{(v_{i}^{train}|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{train})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{train}=\{(v_{i}^{train}|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{train})\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{train}=\{(w_{i}^{train}|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{train})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{train}=\{(w_{i}^{train}|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{train})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Based on the distribution of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{train}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{train}</annotation></semantics></math>, two thresholds, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for absolute falls are determined, where <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the maximum <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> values of ADLs, respectively. Additionally, two thresholds, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ADL}^{Norm_{xyz}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ADL}^{Norm_{xyz}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ADL}^{Norm_{hori}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ADL}^{Norm_{hori}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for the absolute ADL identification are determined, where<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ADL}^{Norm_{xyz}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ADL}^{Norm_{xyz}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{ADL}^{Norm_{hori}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{ADL}^{Norm_{hori}}</annotation></semantics></math> are the minimum <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> values of falls, respectively. Similarly, the maximum and minimum values of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{xyz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{xyz}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Norm_{hori}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Norm_{hori}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{test}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{test}</annotation></semantics></math> are presented as <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m28" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{test}=\{(v_{i}^{test})|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{test}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{test}=\{(v_{i}^{test})|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{test}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m29" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="W_{test}=\{(w_{i}^{test})|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{test}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{test}=\{(w_{i}^{test})|i=1,2,\cdots,N_{test}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Finally, the threshold-based classification (TC) applied to the test set is defined as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle TC(v_{i}^{test},w_{i}^{test})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle TC(v_{i}^{test},w_{i}^{test})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}{\rm Fall,if}\ v_{i}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}{\rm and}\ w_{i}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}\\
{\rm ADL,if}\ v_{i}^{test}&lt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}{\rm and}\ w_{i}^{test}&lt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}\\
{\rm Uncertain,\ others.}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>Fall</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ADL</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>Uncertain</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>others</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}{\rm Fall,if}\ v_{i}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}{\rm and}\ w_{i}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}\\
{\rm ADL,if}\ v_{i}^{test}&lt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{xyz}}{\rm and}\ w_{i}^{test}&lt;T_{fall}^{Norm_{hori}}\\
{\rm Uncertain,\ others.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, three regions are distinguished: the absolute boundary of falls and ADLs, as well as the range of uncertain data that will be transferred to the MEC.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S4.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.03601v1/Visio-Knowledge-Distillation-2Layer.png" id="S4.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/113;" width="333" height="113" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="S4.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.03601v1/Visio-Knowledge-Distillation-3Layer.png" id="S4.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:333/157;" width="333" height="157" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 6: </span>The multilayer MECs with the KD approach. (a) Dual-layer (b) Triple-layer.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Loss Functions of Dual-layer and Triple-layer MECs</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, the loss functions of dual-layer and triple-layer MECs are analyzed.
The architectures of dual-layer and triple-layer MECs with the KD approach are shown in Fig. <a href="#S4.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ IV-B Threshold-Based Classification ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in <a href="#S4.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ IV-B Threshold-Based Classification ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>(a), the teacher model is pre-trained based on the dual-layer MEC architecture.
Then, we use the pre-trained teacher model and ground truth (label) to train the student model.
By this KD approach, the weights of the teacher models are distilled into the student model.
This KD approach improves the performance of the student model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In general, supervised learning uses cross-entropy loss to measure the mismatch between the output of the student model and the ground truth (label) as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="loss={\cal H}(g,Student)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">loss={\cal H}(g,Student).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> represents the ground-truth value, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Student" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Student</annotation></semantics></math> represents the output of the student model, and <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\cal H}(p,q)=-\mathbb{E}_{p}(\log(q))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\cal H}(p,q)=-\mathbb{E}_{p}(\log(q))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">In the dual-layer MECs architecture (teacher-student model), we use the Kullback–Leibler (KL) divergence loss to match the softened outputs of the teacher and student models as follows</p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle KL</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E6Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)\left[\log\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)-\log\left(\frac{Teacher}{T}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)\left[\log\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)-\log\left(\frac{Teacher}{T}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Teacher" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Teacher</annotation></semantics></math> represents the predicted values of the teacher model, <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Student" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Student</annotation></semantics></math> represents the predicted values of the student model, KL represents the KL-divergence between the output probabilities of the <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Teacher" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Teacher</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Student" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Student</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is referred to as an additional control parameter between the ground truth (label) and the soft targets from the output of the teacher model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">The loss function of the student model is as follows</p>
<table id="S4.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle loss_{dual}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle loss_{dual}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda T^{2}\times KL\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda T^{2}\times KL\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E7Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-\lambda)loss)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-\lambda)loss),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter that adjusts the trade-off between two loss functions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>, the TAKD is used to improve the performance of the student model of the teacher-TA-student model, when the performance gap between the teacher and student is large. As shown in <a href="#S4.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ IV-B Threshold-Based Classification ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>(b), the weights of the pre-trained teacher model are extracted and distilled into the TA model. Then, the weights of the pre-trained TA model are further distilled into the student model.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">In the triple-layer MECs architecture, the KD loss function in the teacher-TA-student model is formulated. Firstly, we formulate the first KL divergence between the teacher model and the TA model. Subsequently, the second KL divergence is calculated for the distilled TA model and the student model. The first KL divergence is substituted into the second KL divergence, as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E8X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle KL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle KL</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{TA}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)=\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{TA}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)=\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E8Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\left\{\log\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)-\log\left(\frac{TA}{T}\right)\right.\left.\left[\log\left(\frac{TA}{T}\right)-\log\left(\frac{Teacher}{T}\right)\right]\right\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\left\{\log\left(\frac{Student}{T}\right)-\log\left(\frac{TA}{T}\right)\right.\left.\left[\log\left(\frac{TA}{T}\right)-\log\left(\frac{Teacher}{T}\right)\right]\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TA" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TA</annotation></semantics></math> represents the predicted values of the TA model. Then, we substitute the obtained values into Eq. (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In IV-C Loss Functions of Dual-layer and Triple-layer MECs ‣ IV DL-based FD with KD in MLMEC Framework ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to calculate the loss function of the student model in the triple-layer MECs architecture as follows</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle loss_{tri}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle loss_{tri}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda T^{2}\times KL\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{TA}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda T^{2}\times KL\left(\frac{Teacher}{T},\frac{TA}{T},\frac{Student}{T}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+(1-\lambda)loss." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(1-\lambda)loss.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">IV-D</span> </span><span id="S4.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Threshold-Based Judgment for Uncertain Data</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For processing the uncertain data of the previous layer MEC, a threshold-based judgment is proposed to distinguish absolute falls, ADL, and uncertain data. We define two threshold values, namely maximum and minimum upward thresholds <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{fall}^{Max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{fall}^{Max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{fall}^{Min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{fall}^{Min}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are preset to define the range of the absolute falls, ADL, and uncertain data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">If the result of the judgment remains uncertain, the data is sent to the larger model in the upper-layer MEC for a more precise detection. After the softmax function in the DL model of the <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer MEC, the softened output is obtained as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{n}^{test}={\rm softmax}\left(\frac{Layer_{n}}{T}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{n}^{test}={\rm softmax}\left(\frac{Layer_{n}}{T}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Layer_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Layer_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the predicted result of the <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer MEC. Then, we input the softened output of the <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th layer MEC to the threshold-based upward judgment (<math id="S4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TQ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TQ</annotation></semantics></math>), which is defined as follows</p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TQ(v_{j}^{test})=\begin{cases}{\rm Fall,\;if}\ v_{n}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Max}\\
{\rm ADL,\;if}\ v_{n}^{test}&lt;T_{fall}^{Min}\\
{\rm Uncertain,\;if}\ T_{fall}^{Max}&gt;v_{n}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Min}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>Fall</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>ADL</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>Uncertain</mi><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>if</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TQ(v_{j}^{test})=\begin{cases}{\rm Fall,\;if}\ v_{n}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Max}\\
{\rm ADL,\;if}\ v_{n}^{test}&lt;T_{fall}^{Min}\\
{\rm Uncertain,\;if}\ T_{fall}^{Max}&gt;v_{n}^{test}&gt;T_{fall}^{Min}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Performance Evaluation</span></h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The performance evaluation of the FD system was carried out using the leave-one-out cross-validation method. In this approach, data from one subject served as the test set while the data from the other subjects were used as the training set. This process was repeated <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> times, where <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of subjects, ensuring that each subject’s data was used as the test set. After all iterations, the overall test results are aggregated, and the average performance of the <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> Folds is considered as the final output for evaluating the performance of the FD system.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Applying the concept of a confusion matrix, four performance metrics are introduced, including accuracy (<math id="S5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ACC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ACC</annotation></semantics></math>), precision (<math id="S5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PRE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PRE</annotation></semantics></math>), recall (<math id="S5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="REC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">REC</annotation></semantics></math>), and F1-score (<math id="S5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F1</annotation></semantics></math>), to measure the detection performance. The definitions of performance metrics are as follows:</p>
<table id="S5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle ACC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle ACC</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{TP+TN}{TP+FP+TN+FN}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{TP+TN}{TP+FP+TN+FN},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle PRE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle PRE</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{TP}{TP+FP}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{TP}{TP+FP},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle REC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle REC</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{TP}{TP+FN}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{TP}{TP+FN},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle F1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle F1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{PRE\times REC}{PRE+REC}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{PRE\times REC}{PRE+REC},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where True Positive (<math id="S5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TP</annotation></semantics></math>) refers to instances where fall signals are correctly identified as falls. True Negative (<math id="S5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="TN" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">TN</annotation></semantics></math>) indicates instances where activities of daily living (ADLs) signals are correctly identified as ADLs. False Positive (<math id="S5.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FP" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FP</annotation></semantics></math>) represents instances where ADL signals are incorrectly labeled as falls, while False Negative (<math id="S5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="FN" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">FN</annotation></semantics></math>) denotes instances where fall signals are incorrectly labeled as ADLs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, the latency evaluation of each MEC of the MLMEC framework is calculated. The latency of the MLMEC architecture is defined as the total computation and transmission time from the ED to the CC. From ED to CC, each layer of the MLMEC framework processes incoming data from the previous layer. Therefore, the latency between ED and CC is expressed as</p>
<table id="S5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{M_{n-1}}\sum_{i\in Q_{n-1}^{j}}\left[\frac{s_{n}^{i}b_{n}^{i}}{\theta_{n}^{i}}+\frac{\rho s_{n}^{i}\lambda_{n}^{i}+(1-s_{n}^{i})\lambda_{n}^{i}+\beta_{n}^{i}}{\varphi_{n}^{j,i}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{n}=\sum_{j=1}^{M_{n-1}}\sum_{i\in Q_{n-1}^{j}}\left[\frac{s_{n}^{i}b_{n}^{i}}{\theta_{n}^{i}}+\frac{\rho s_{n}^{i}\lambda_{n}^{i}+(1-s_{n}^{i})\lambda_{n}^{i}+\beta_{n}^{i}}{\varphi_{n}^{j,i}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The notation definitions are provided in Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Notations of latency calculation.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:333.0pt;height:74.7pt;vertical-align:-35.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-55.5pt,12.5pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
<table id="S5.T2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variable</span></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The number of devices on each layer <math id="S5.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{n-1}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{n-1}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The number of child nodes connected with the parent node <math id="S5.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> on layer <math id="S5.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Data generation speed of ED <math id="S5.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The total volume of the processed data received by node <math id="S5.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on layer <math id="S5.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The (equivalent) task division percentage at node <math id="S5.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on layer <math id="S5.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The computing capacity of node <math id="S5.T2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on layer <math id="S5.T2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.1.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{n}^{j,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>φ</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{n}^{j,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T2.1.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T2.1.1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The transmitting capacity of node <math id="S5.T2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on layer <math id="S5.T2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to its parent node <math id="S5.T2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experimental Results and Discussions</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our simulations, FallAllD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> and SisFall <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite> datasets were chosen to validate the proposed MLMEC FD system and the KD approach for managing the trade-off between accuracy and latency.
These two datasets were collected from real-life fall types and ADLs, and the sampling rates are 200 Hz.
We set the window sizes of the sub-windows before and after the impact point (i.e., <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WS_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WS_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="WS_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">WS_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>), respectively, to be 2 seconds (s) and 1.23 s for the FallAllD dataset, and 2 s and 1.44 s for the SisFall dataset. Our previous study <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">44</a>]</cite> has shown that such window size settings achieved optimal performance of the proposed FD systems for these two public datasets.
Pytorch 1.13.0 is used on a 64-bit Windows 10 PC with an Intel 13th Gen I7-13700K CPU 3.40GHz and an Nvidia RTX4080 GPU with 16GB dedicated memory. The data pre-processing and DL-based modeling were performed in an Anaconda environment.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S6.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">VI-A</span> </span><span id="S6.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Open Datasets</span></h3>

<section id="S6.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.4" class="ltx_text">VI-A</span>1 </span>FallAllD Dataset</h4>

<div id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">M. Saleh <span id="S6.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al.</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> proposed a public dataset that involved placing an inertial measurement unit (IMU) on the neck, chest, and waist to capture various types of falls during both non-activity and activity. Each IMU included a triaxial accelerometer, gyroscope, magnetometer, and barometer. Fifteen healthy young participants took part in the study, providing a total of 1053 ADLs and 425 fall trials. Accelerometer data from the waist was the focus due to its prominence and ease of distinction. Tab. <a href="#S6.T3" title="TABLE III ‣ VI-A1 FallAllD Dataset ‣ VI-A Open Datasets ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">III</span></a> shows the details of the FallAllD dataset. The FallAllD dataset comprised 15 healthy young participants, encompassing eight males and seven females, aged between 21 and 53 years, weighing between 48 and 85 kg, and measuring in height from 158 to 187 cm. The average age, height, and weight were 32 years, 171 cm, and 67 kg, respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE III: </span>The information on participation in the FallAllD dataset</figcaption>
