<div id="S6.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure the applicability of uncertain data in real-world scenarios, the concept of a threshold is proposed during the testing phase, utilizing the softmax output judgment process.
The data were categorized into three groups: fall types, ADLs, and uncertain data.
If the detection of the current MEC layer is classified as uncertain, it is sent to the next MEC layer.
For example, if the softmax output of the current layer is larger than the maximum threshold value (0.8 in this study), it represents a fall type. Conversely, if the output falls below the minimum threshold value (0.2 in this study), it represents ADLs.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S6.T9" title="TABLE IX ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IX</span></a> and Table <a href="#S6.T10" title="TABLE X ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">X</span></a> present the data amount of each layer in the MLMEC under different threshold settings by using the FallAllD and Sisfall datasets. The FallAllD dataset contains 1,428,600 testing data points, while the SisFall dataset has 2,463,200 testing data points.</p>
</div>
