<div id="S6.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The preset threshold values were chosen to maximize the resource efficiency of the MECs.
Based on the threshold-based judgment for uncertain data, the amounts of data in each layer were compared, as shown in Tables <a href="#S6.T11" title="TABLE XI ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XI</span></a>, <a href="#S6.T12" title="TABLE XII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XII</span></a>, and <a href="#S6.T13" title="TABLE XIII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XIII</span></a>.
In addition to comparing the amounts of processed data, the latency of each layer was calculated.
The parameters <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> Eq. <a href="#S5.E16" title="In V Performance Evaluation ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> represent the data transmission rates per second and the parameters <math id="S6.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{n}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{n}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the CPU computation loads.</p>
</div>
