</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The latencies of the dual-layer and triple-layer MECs architecture without KD are presented in Table <a href="#S6.T11" title="TABLE XI ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XI</span></a> and Table <a href="#S6.T12" title="TABLE XII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XII</span></a>, respectively.
Since the dual-layer only has the latency from MEC 1 to CC, the latency from MEC 1 to MEC 2 of the triple-layer is used to compare. The improvement in latency is approximately 4.64%.</p>
</div>
