</figure>
<div id="S6.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#S6.T12" title="TABLE XII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XII</span></a> and Table <a href="#S6.T13" title="TABLE XIII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XIII</span></a>, we compare the amount of data with and without KD using two datasets.
Using the FallAllD dataset, the data amount for the CC was reduced by 34%, while that for MEC 2 was reduced by 61%. In the Sisfall dataset, the data amount for the CC was reduced by 71%, while that for MEC 2 was reduced by 48%.
In addition, the latency of the MLMEC architecture is calculated by Eq. <a href="#S5.E16" title="In V Performance Evaluation ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>.
By comparing Table <a href="#S6.T12" title="TABLE XII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XII</span></a> and Table <a href="#S6.T13" title="TABLE XIII ‣ VI-D Comparison of the Student Models ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XIII</span></a>, the latency of the MLMEC with KD exhibits a significant reduction compared to that without KD.
Specifically, latency was remarkably reduced by 54.15% for the FallAllD dataset and by 46.67% for the SisFall dataset.
This indicates that if falls are detected at MEC 1 or MEC 2, there is no need to upload the data to the CC for further detection, thereby reducing computational costs and improving efficiency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S6.SS5.4" class="ltx_text">VI-E</span> </span><span id="S6.SS5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Min-Max Normalization and Z-Score Standardization</span></h3>

<div id="S6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">N. A. Choudhury <span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al.</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> and H. Henderi <span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">et al.</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite> compared the detection performance by using min-max normalization and z-score standardization. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>, the obtained test results using min-max normalization and z-score standardization have similar performance in terms of accuracy rate. In <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>]</cite>, the obtained test results using min-max normalization outperform z-score standardization in terms of accuracy rate. Based on the testing result that shows min-max normalization outperforms z-score standardization in terms of <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ACC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ACC</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="REC" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">REC</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PRE" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PRE</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math>1 score as shown in Tab. <a href="#S6.T14" title="TABLE XIV ‣ VI-E Min-Max Normalization and Z-Score Standardization ‣ VI Experimental Results and Discussions ‣ MECKD: Deep Learning-Based Fall Detection in Multilayer Mobile Edge Computing With Knowledge Distillation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">XIV</span></a>, we chose the min-max normalization in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE XIV: </span>Comparison of min-max normalization and z-score standardization.</figcaption>
<div id="S6.T14.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:291.4pt;height:78.9pt;vertical-align:-37.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-16.2pt,4.4pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<table id="S6.T14.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S6.T14.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T14.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Methods</span></td>
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T14.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DL Models</span></td>
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ACC_{imp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ACC_{imp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="REC_{imp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">REC_{imp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PRC_{imp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PRC_{imp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><math id="S6.T14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F1_{imp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F1_{imp}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" rowspan="3"><span id="S6.T14.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Min-max</span></td>
<td id="S6.T14.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">ResNet18</td>
